 "about_text": "AISHO is a Japanese gallery originally established in Hong Kong in 2012 as AISHONANZUKA, later renamed AISHO Hong Kong, with a Tokyo branch opening in 2024. Founded by Aisho Miura, the gallery is rooted in street art and focuses on introducing non-academic, non-mainstream creative talents to Asian and global audiences. Its program bridges diverse cultures and explores emerging markets across East Asia. AISHO represents a wide roster of international and Japanese artists, including figures such as Hajime Sorayama, Javier Calleja, Keiichi Tanaami, and Yoon Hyup, alongside street-art-oriented artists like Cyril Kongo and Joakim Ojanen. The gallery has participated in major international art fairs including the Armory Show, Art Basel Hong Kong, Miami, and Basel, and Frieze London.",
